    "q-73069": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73069",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The area under the curve $y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ between $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $4$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?",
      "worked_solution": "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're given that $n=4$ subintervals.  The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0)}{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{4-1}f(0+j\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}f(\\frac{j\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
