    "q-49383": {
      "dom_id": "step-q49383",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The area under the curve $y=5-{x}^{2}$ between $x=-1$ and $x=1$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?",
      "worked_solution": "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of subintervals, ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$, and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nThe endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=1,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-(-1)}{n}=\\frac{2}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(-1+j\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(-1+\\frac{2j}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[5-{(-1+\\frac{2j}{n})}^{2}]\\frac{2}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{2}{n}(4+\\frac{4j}{n}-\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{{n}^{2}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-49383-a",
