    "q-315710": {
      "dom_id": "step-q315710",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+1)$ between $x=-1$ and $x=2$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j$ and $n.$*\n\n${S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡($\n{{field-1}} $)$",
      "worked_solution": "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-(-1)}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[f(-1+j\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(-1+\\frac{3j}{n})+1)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6j}{n}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
