      "source_example_id": "e-402",
      "knowledge_point": "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation",
      "kp_id": "e-402"
    },
    "q-345052": {
      "dom_id": "step-q345052",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14223189/assets/f321b063e3bc76eeb5b426d00cbf94451a06cec928008eaadc965547691c412a.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=4+x$ between $x=0,$ $x=4$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a right Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $i.$*\n\n${S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}($\n{{field-1}} $)$",
      "worked_solution": "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=4$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=4,$ so the step size is \n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-0}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(0+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(i) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4+i).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
