    },
    "q-116626": {
      "dom_id": "step-q116626",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "The area under the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+2}$ between $x=-2$ and $x=2$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $7$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?",
      "worked_solution": "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is   \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n=7$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=-2$ and $b=2.$ So, the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-(-2)}{7}=\\frac{4}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}f(-2+i\\cdot \\frac{4}{7})\\cdot \\frac{4}{7} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}f(-2+\\frac{4i}{7})\\cdot \\frac{4}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{(-2+\\frac{4i}{7})+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{4i}{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
