    "q-345038": {
      "dom_id": "step-q345038",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "The area under the curve $y=(x+1)^{2}$ between $x=-1$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $4$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $i.$*\n\n${S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is   \n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n=4$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=3.$ So, the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-(-1)}{4}=\\frac{4}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(-1+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(-1+i)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}\\,{(-1+i+1)}^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}\\,{i}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
