    "q-49364": {
      "dom_id": "step-q49364",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ between $x=0$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?",
      "worked_solution": "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[f(0+j\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[f(\\frac{3j}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3j}{n})].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
